{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>His firstborn ox.</b> This is Joseph — the firstborn ox of the Dweller of the bush — for even though the kingship belongs to Judah, who is called a lion, Joseph nonetheless ranks after him in precedence just as the ox ranks after the lion, as the Sages said (Ḥagigah 13a): the king among beasts is the lion; among domestic animals, the ox. By this, the tribe of Joseph was first among the tribes after the tribe of Judah, as it says: כִּדְבַר אֶפְרַיִם רְתֵת (Hosea 13:1)." "<b>His splendor.</b> Even though he lacks the majesty of kingship, he is worthy of splendor and precedence." "<b>With them he shall gore peoples together.</b> Together with the ruling tribe he shall destroy many peoples, as it says: וְסָרָה קִנְאַת אֶפְרַיִם וְצֹרְרֵי יְהוּדָה יִכָּרֵתוּ, וְעָפוּ בְכָתֵף פְּלִשְׁתִּים יָמָּה, יַחְדָּיו יָבֹזּוּ אֶת בְּנֵי קֶדֶם (Isaiah 11:13–14)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {0 "Reading שֶׁל שׁוֹכְנִי סְנֶה as 'of the Dweller of the bush,' referring to the One who dwelt in the burning bush (Deut. 33:16)."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:23:39.294928989Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}